# Home Lab Telegram bot — ids permitted to invoke PRIVILEGED commands.
#
# Installed to /etc/homelab-telegram-bot/privileged-allowlist
#
# This is AUTHORISATION, and it is a different question from the one
# `allowlist` answers.
#
#   allowlist             may this user talk to the bot at all?   (authentication)
#   privileged-allowlist  may this user invoke /restart?          (authorisation)
#
# Every id here MUST also appear in `allowlist`. The bot enforces that at
# startup and refuses to run otherwise: a user cannot be authorised for
# privileged commands without first being permitted to use the bot.
#
# EMPTY IS FINE AND MEANS "NOBODY MAY ESCALATE".
#
# Note this is the opposite of `allowlist`, where empty is fatal. The asymmetry
# is deliberate: empty-means-nobody fails safe, empty-means-everybody does not.

# 123456789
